# build output, at any depth: a crate built on its own (an excluded fork) makes one of its own.
# The laws' reader skips target/ and node_modules/ wherever they sit, and this file is what makes
# that honest: the repository never holds them (tools/leis, L1 asks git).
target/
# web frontends keep their modules local; a dist/ is committed when a crate embeds it
**/node_modules
# Python leftovers (abaco's macros, scripts)
__pycache__/
# editor state
.vs/
*.user
# proprietary vendor documents stay machine-local (docs/questions.md Q6)
docs/vendor/*
!docs/vendor/README.md
